<title>SINGAPORE: World rice prices - December 5.</title>
<headline>World rice prices - December 5.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rice prices quoted by trading and official sources in the key producing nations of Thailand, Vietnam, India and the United States in U.S. dollars a tonne:</p>
<p>							     Dec 5     Nov 28</p>
<p>Thailand-100 pct white B benchmark FOB Bangkok 325-350  318-350 Thailand-100 pct fragrant rice			615     600-615</p>
<p>India-25 pct broken(non-Basmati long grain)FOB  235	 240</p>
<p>India-15-10 pct broken FOB (west coast port)  250-290   260-290</p>
<p>Vietnam-5.0 percent broken FOB Saigon port	280     280-290</p>
<p>Vietnam-10 percent broken FOB Saigon port	 270     275-280</p>
<p>U.S.-California medium grain ($ per cwt) 19.50-20.50 19.50-20.50</p>
<p>U.S.-Long grain Arkansas ($ per cwt)     19.50-20.00 19.50-20.00</p>
<p>- Singapore Newsroom (65-8703305)</p>
